Rockchip RK3588 secure boot keys

Files
  dev.key: RSA 2048-bit private key for signing IDBlock, Loader, U-Boot FIT and kernel FIT.
  dev.pubkey: Matching PEM public key used by Rockchip rk_sign_tool.
  dev.crt: Matching X.509 certificate used by the U-Boot FIT signing tools.
  All three files must use the same RSA key pair, separate from the OTA keys.

Boards already provisioned with a public key hash require the original matching
private key. The commands below create a new signing identity; do not replace the
keys used by a board whose public key hash has already been fused.

Generate a key pair
  Run these commands in a new, empty directory:

  umask 077
  openssl genrsa -traditional -out dev.key 2048
  openssl rsa -in dev.key -pubout -out dev.pubkey
  openssl req -new -x509 -key dev.key -sha256 -days 3650 \
    -subj '/CN=NAOS RK3588 Secure Boot/' -out dev.crt
  chmod 600 dev.key

Verify that the public keys match
  All three commands must produce the same SHA256 digest. This is the digest of
  the public key in SPKI DER format, not the Rockchip public key hash for OTP:

  openssl pkey -in dev.key -pubout -outform DER | sha256sum
  openssl pkey -pubin -in dev.pubkey -outform DER | sha256sum
  openssl x509 -in dev.crt -pubkey -noout | openssl pkey -pubin -outform DER | sha256sum
